course: dictionary
lesson: 9899
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word talent has three. The usual one is a natural ability to do something well, like singing, drawing or sport. «A talent show» lets pupils sing, dance, tell jokes or do tricks, so talent means an ability that people show off.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In a talent show, the pupils are showing what they can do well, so talent must mean ability. Check it: swap in the word ability and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Be careful with old meanings. «In the Parable of the Talents, a talent was a large sum of money.» The clues are sum and the servants who trade money. Long ago, a talent was a heavy weight of silver or gold used as money. Always read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: A talent is a natural ability to do something well, like singing, drawing or sport.
fact: Talent can also mean people with abilities, as in «new talent», which means fresh young performers.
fact: Useful phrases: «a talent for», «talent show», «natural talent», «hidden talent».
fact: In ancient times, a talent was a large weight of silver or gold, used as money.
fact: Teachers often say everyone has talents, and practice grows skill: talent alone is not enough.
exercise: «In the Parable of the Talents, a talent was a large sum of money.» What does talent mean here? | *A large sum of money in ancient times | A school show | Natural ability to sing or draw | A cheap toy
exercise: Mia draws better than anyone in her class. Which phrase fits best? | a talent show | *a natural talent for drawing | a hidden door | a large sum of money
exercise: Teachers say practice grows skill, and talent alone is not enough. What does this tell you? | *Practice matters as well as a natural gift | Only talent matters, and practice does not | Talent is a kind of food | Skill and talent are always the same thing
test: What does a «talent show» let pupils do? | *Sing, dance, tell jokes or do tricks | Sell old silver | Sleep in class | A test in maths
test: Which phrase means a natural ability, not money? | *natural talent | a heavy weight of gold | a hidden purse | a large sum
exam: «TV talent shows are edited to be dramatic, so harsh comments and tears are often shown.» What does this suggest? | They always show every moment exactly as it happened | *Some scenes are chosen to be exciting, so they may not show everything | They are only for adults | They are very boring
